+`encode` flattens the current position for model inputs: 64 squares in square
+order (index 0 is a1, index 63 is h8), castling rights, only legally
+usable en passant, the counters and the repetition count. `--relative` mirrors
+the board vertically and swaps colours when Black is to move, so the side to
+move is always uppercase and moves up the board; `fen` and `side_to_move` stay
+absolute.
+
 `dead_position: null` means unknown, not false. The v1 recognizer handles only
 three elementary material patterns plus kings with bishops that all stand on
 one square colour. `terminal_reason: null` therefore means no
